name issue_12_lossbwe_high_jitter_no_loss
describe 40 ms jitter with reordering and no loss: reordered packets must not read as loss (#12, #19)
# A packet counts as lost only when a feedback message covers it and reports it as not received, and a
# later report of it as received removes it again (LossBasedBweV2::PushBackObservation). `tcc v2` is
# libwebrtc's feedback generator, which reports a reordered packet again; with `tcc v1` (each arrival
# reported once) the late packets stay lost and the average loss reads 16 % on this link.
# 5 seeds (cc v2, tcc v2): average reported loss 2.5 %,
# cc.target_avg_kbps 107-437. Target (parity): libwebrtc 1003 kbps; what is left is
# the delay detector (#24), not the loss path.
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
# PR for #518 (harness: our session's timers at their due microsecond, as libwebrtc's on SimTime; program.md 0.2, for the
# Coordinator): was == 0. Ours 227 on seed 1 (seeds 1-10: 227 on 1, 262 on 9, 0 on the rest); libwebrtc 0 on seeds 1-10.
# Seed 1's freeze is at 29.5 s, where the render time catches up with frames that ran 300+ ms late since 20 s (frames
# delayed by retransmission skip UpdateCurrentDelay, on both stacks: libwebrtc's longest gaps on seed 1 are 168 and 162 ms,
# its e2e p95 361 ms against ~150 on the other seeds); seed 9's is at start-up, after the pacer released frame 600 100 ms later.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 300
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.concealed_pct < 2
expect cc.target_avg_kbps > 100
